{
 "manufacturer": "Siemens",
 "manufacturer_slug": "siemens",
 "model": "SENTRON WL (3WL) air circuit breaker with COM16 Modbus module",
 "model_slug": "sentron-3wl-com16",
 "short_model": "SENTRON 3WL COM16",
 "aliases": [
  "SENTRON WL",
  "3WL",
  "3WL COM16",
  "COM16"
 ],
 "equipment_type": "Circuit breaker trip unit (power meter)",
 "applies_to": "Siemens SENTRON 3WL air circuit breakers with a COM16 Modbus RTU communication module and, for voltage/power/energy values, the metering function (PLUS), per system manual A5E02126891-02.",
 "summary": "SENTRON WL breakers talk Modbus RTU through the COM16 module. Data is grouped in register blocks: the high byte of the register number is the block (data set) number, e.g. block 94 at 0x5E01 holds the live measured values. This map covers the 16-bit and 32-bit measured values of block 94, the min/max blocks 72-76, the counters of block 91 and a few overview values of block 51.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": 126,
  "baud": 19200,
  "parity": "None",
  "data_bits": null,
  "stop_bits": null,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "1-based",
  "note": "The register-block tables print 1-based register numbers in decimal and hex, where the high byte is the block number (block 94 starts at 0x5E01). The manual's write example for block 68 sends start address 0x4402 for the system time, which the block 68 table lists at 0x4403, so the wire address is the printed number minus 1."
 },
 "default_word_order": "ABCD",
 "firmware": null,
 "source": {
  "title": "SENTRON 3WL/3VL circuit breakers with communication capability - Modbus, System Manual",
  "doc_number": "A5E02126891-02",
  "revision_date": "2011-07",
  "url": "https://assets.new.siemens.com/siemens/assets/api/uuid:2216d539-488d-4320-b10a-d79f984e4a75/manual-modbus-sentron-3wl-3vl-en.pdf",
  "pages": "pp. 129-143 (Modbus RTU functions and examples), p. 157-159 (scaling, units), pp. 182-213 (WL register blocks 51, 72-76, 91, 92, 94), p. 243 (data formats)"
 },
 "notes": [
  "Scaling in the tables is a power-of-ten exponent applied at the master (e.g. frequency -2 means x 0.01); it is converted to a plain multiplier here.",
  "The data-format chapter says all Modbus RTU data is sent in Motorola (big-endian) format; 32-bit 'unsigned long' values (energies, runtime meter) are mapped high word first.",
  "Units follow the manual's default unit table (A, V, kW, kVA, kvar, Hz, s); energies carry the unit printed in their name.",
  "Left out: byte-packed values (one register holding two 8-bit items, e.g. unbalance %, THD, form/peak factor, temperatures), 64-bit time stamps, logs, harmonics, format-coded status words and all property bytes.",
  "Voltage, power, energy, power factor and frequency need the breaker's metering function or metering function PLUS; currents come from the electronic trip unit (ETU).",
  "The value buffer area is read with function 03 and written with 16; basic type data, control bytes and status bits use functions 04, 01/05/15 and 02.",
  "SENTRON 3VL moulded-case breakers use different data areas (section 8.8) and are not covered by this map.",
  "The kWh/kvarh energy registers of block 94 (0x5E3B-0x5E41) have no scaling entry in the table and are left out; the MWh/Mvarh versions are included.",
  "Byte order inside a register is high byte first in the function 03/04 examples; the function 16 system-time example labels its bytes differently, but that only concerns byte-packed values, which are left out here."
 ],
